# Book: Tests/Bugs/FORT-555217-VeryLongIdentifier.versetest:11 (untagged; :5
# has a 7000-character type name): a name of 4096 characters. The Book
# refuses it on both VMs as a semantic error, 3655. The survey counts :5 and
# :11 as agreeing only because OpenVerse refuses something else in them (an
# unknown type, an unknown attribute): OpenVerse has no limit on a name's
# length, admits this field and prints
#   field 42
# If UEFN 43.12 refuses it, OpenVerse needs a length limit somewhere between
# 1025 (long-ident-1025) and 4096 characters. Run it alone (single mode),
# not in a batch: Epic's names for it may depend on the module that holds
# it.
# Epic's compiler (UEFN 43.12, ++Fortnite+Release-43.12-CL-60598086,
# BuildAll, 2026-11-19) refuses it: 3655 (L12) "Identifier is too long";
# 3655 (L17) "Identifier is too long".
longer_field := class:
    :int = 42
    F(P:int):int = P

Main():void =
    Obj := longer_field{}
    Print("OVPROBE field {Obj.}")
